{#
  The Codepedia mark, inlined in both variants (036 spec FR-014, FR-015).

  Both are emitted and CSS decides which is visible, rather than swapping an
  `<img src>` from JavaScript. That buys three things at once:

    * Nothing is fetched, so constitution 2.2 and FR-022 hold by construction -
      there is no request to fail, block or leak.
    * The swap works with no JavaScript at all, so the correct mark is showing
      before `wiki-ui.js` parses, and stays correct if it never loads.
    * An `<img>` cannot respond to a `data-theme` attribute on an ancestor,
      which is what the theme actually sets.

  Total cost is under 2 KB per page; the favicon, at ~5.5 KB, is copied into
  assets/ instead for exactly that reason (research.md §3, §4).

  Copied verbatim from docs/brand/codepedia-mark-{light,dark}.svg with three
  edits, all required and none cosmetic:

    * `role`, `aria-label` and `<title>` are stripped and the wrapper is
      `aria-hidden="true"`. The brand slot already carries a *visible*
      "codepedia" wordmark, and as published a screen reader would announce the
      name twice (FR-019). The placeholder this replaces was already aria-hidden.
    * `width`/`height` are dropped so the 24 px box sizes it. The published
      files are 256 px square; the viewBox is what preserves the geometry.
    * `xmlns` is dropped. An inline `<svg>` in an HTML document is put in the
      SVG namespace by the HTML parser itself, so the attribute is redundant
      here - it is only required in a standalone .svg file or in XHTML. It also
      contains the literal `http://www.w3.org/2000/svg`, which trips the
      zero-network guards in tests/integration/test_mermaid_diagram.py and
      test_wiki_ui_assets.py. Those guards are blunt on purpose and worth
      keeping that way, and a namespace declaration is never fetched, so
      removing the redundant attribute is the correct fix rather than
      loosening them.
    * Nothing else. Fills stay exactly as published - #14274A / #FFFFFF and
      their inverse - because the brand README forbids recolouring the lens, and
      the two-tone contrast is what keeps the mark readable at this size
      (FR-018). Do not "simplify" these to currentColor.

  This file must stay a *.jinja file directly in this directory:
  `template_fingerprint()` globs TEMPLATES_DIR non-recursively for *.jinja only,
  so artwork moved to a subdirectory or a .svg sidecar would become invisible to
  the staleness check, and editing it would leave every already-generated page
  stale with no signal (research.md §6, contract invariant 7).
#}
